Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?fix(pricing):=20GEO-005a=20=E2=80=94=20the=20ba?=
 =?UTF-8?q?nd=20is=20a=20parameter,=20not=20a=20field?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Unblocks the production build. 9305471 landed the first cut of GEO-005, which
put `band` inside EstimateInput. That interface is also the argument to
describeFloorForChat and bookMeasureIntent, which write a sentence about a floor
and must not know a price, so both failed tsc --noEmit and the Vercel build
exited 1.

The band is now the estimator's second argument. Same behaviour, same numbers,
465 tests and 66 guards green — describing a floor and pricing one are separate
concerns again and cannot drift into each other.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Wz3f94TUzSk49wD2izgQYx
