--
--Closes GC-025, found the day the floor studio shipped.
--
--FLOORING_RATES_CAD_PER_SQFT in packages/shared/ai was a second price source,
--never derived from PRICE_BANDS. Four of its six install rates fell outside the
--published band — red oak $2/sq ft under the floor, maple $1 under, engineered
--$3 under, black walnut $4 over the ceiling — and refinishing missed the
--published full-sand band at both ends. It reached the configurator, /design, the
--spec sheet, /api/estimate, /api/chat and /floor-studio, which is linked from the
--header and footer of every page.
--
--The finish and pattern multipliers on top of it were labelled in the file as
--PLACEHOLDERS that were 'NOT Ecowoods real numbers', with a warning that the site
--would otherwise 'quote prices nobody has agreed to honour'. The owner confirmed
--on 2026-09-12 that they are not rates he would honour.
--
--The table and both multiplier sets are deleted. estimateInstalledRangeCad now
--takes a PublishedBand and multiplies it by an area; it calculates no rate.
--packages/shared is upstream of apps/web, so the band travels in via
--bandForWork(work, country) rather than the constants travelling out.
--
--Removing the invented numbers exposed one live claim built on them: the 'best
--value' explainer reported 'the pattern and finish add roughly N%', a percentage
--that was the placeholder multipliers restated as a fact about money. It now
--ranks the cut by the labour the catalogue itself describes and says where that
--shows up — inside the band, in the written price after the measure.
--
--Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
--Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Wz3f94TUzSk49wD2izgQYx
